WEBVTT

00:04.520 --> 00:06.320
[EREN TITAN growls]

00:06.350 --> 00:09.590
[EREN] I can win.
I can beat Reiner.

00:09.620 --> 00:12.490
He's going down!

00:12.520 --> 00:15.560
[Bellows]

00:15.590 --> 00:20.000
[CONNY]
Huh? No, no, no, no, no!

00:20.030 --> 00:23.800
[MALE SOLDIER 32A]
Above you! Look out!

00:31.980 --> 00:35.380
[SOLDIERS groan]

00:35.410 --> 00:36.980
[BOTH groan]

00:40.520 --> 00:41.890
[MIKASA grunts]

00:41.920 --> 00:43.450
[SOLDIERS scream]

00:43.490 --> 00:46.720
[ALL grunt]

00:49.060 --> 00:56.400
[Roars]

01:05.410 --> 01:11.010
[REINER TITAN growls]

01:11.050 --> 01:13.020
[Gasps]

01:42.850 --> 01:46.350
Eren!

01:49.420 --> 01:54.390
♪ Opening Song ♪

03:38.480 --> 03:45.590
[PYXIS snoring]

03:45.620 --> 03:47.790
[ANKA]
Ugh.

03:47.820 --> 03:51.490
You're kidding me.
Wake up, Commander.

03:51.530 --> 03:54.790
You'll catch your death
sleeping out here.

03:54.830 --> 03:57.630
Tell me you didn't
drink all this yourself.

03:57.670 --> 03:59.800
God. Sir, please.

03:59.830 --> 04:01.770
Keep tossing it back like
someone half your age,

04:01.800 --> 04:03.940
I'll end up
putting you in diapers.

04:03.970 --> 04:05.710
Doesn't sound so bad to me.

04:05.740 --> 04:08.310
Old men like to be doted on.

04:08.340 --> 04:10.240
What's the situation?

04:11.680 --> 04:13.850
Well, several patrol
units were sent out.

04:13.880 --> 04:15.480
Not many Titans
between the first

04:15.520 --> 04:17.550
and second defensive lines.

04:17.590 --> 04:18.850
And the few that did crop up

04:18.890 --> 04:20.950
seemed like they
were pretty far apart.

04:20.990 --> 04:22.460
[PYXIS]
Hmm.

04:22.490 --> 04:24.420
If Hannes and the
advance squad have managed

04:24.460 --> 04:26.530
to follow the wall
without incident,

04:26.560 --> 04:30.260
they should be getting
back before too long.

04:30.300 --> 04:32.400
Fairly straightforward
operation.

04:32.430 --> 04:34.500
They'd have run into
the unit from Krolva

04:34.540 --> 04:37.970
about halfway and
turned around for home.

04:38.010 --> 04:42.380
It's a safe assumption they
encountered few Titans, if any.

04:42.410 --> 04:44.840
If Wall Rose
had been breached,

04:44.880 --> 04:47.650
sightings wouldn't be so random.

04:50.590 --> 04:51.820
[ERWIN]
Commander Pyxis.

04:51.850 --> 04:53.520
[PYXIS]
Hm?

04:53.560 --> 04:56.820
Ah, Commander Erwin.

04:56.860 --> 04:58.860
Is it true what I hear
about you catching

04:58.890 --> 05:00.630
a troublesome little mouse?

05:00.660 --> 05:02.960
Well... technically, yes.

05:03.000 --> 05:04.900
Not that it's helped us.

05:04.930 --> 05:08.600
Hm. Well, at least
those goons in the interior

05:08.640 --> 05:10.570
might start using their heads.

05:10.610 --> 05:13.610
Might even be forced to
reconsider their belief system.

05:13.640 --> 05:15.980
Morally bankrupt as it is.

05:16.010 --> 05:18.750
[ERWIN]
Agreed. Seems they have.

05:18.780 --> 05:20.780
Look over there.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.520
Military Police
putting in an appearance

05:23.550 --> 05:26.690
where Titans aren't just
an academic problem.

05:28.290 --> 05:29.390
[MALE SOLDIER 33A]
Damn. Can't believe

05:29.420 --> 05:31.290
we didn't see one.

05:31.330 --> 05:33.330
You really sayin'
there weren't any?

05:33.360 --> 05:34.590
I know, right?

05:34.630 --> 05:37.000
It's unusually quiet out there.

05:40.640 --> 05:42.740
Wonder if
they're still alive.

05:42.770 --> 05:44.470
What a joke.
I thought this was

05:44.510 --> 05:46.040
s'posed to be an emergency.

05:46.070 --> 05:49.040
Yeah. We just come here
to sit on our asses, or what?

05:49.080 --> 05:53.750
Hey Levi! Where you
hidin' all the Titans?

05:53.780 --> 05:55.250
Problem?

05:55.280 --> 05:57.650
You seem eager to be
eaten alive, solider.

05:57.690 --> 05:58.890
[ALL gasp]

05:58.920 --> 06:01.250
[LEVI] Huh. Sorry we
couldn't make that happen

06:01.290 --> 06:03.790
for you today.
Plenty of opportunities

06:03.830 --> 06:05.960
outside the wall
if you're lookin'.

06:05.990 --> 06:09.500
Lots of scouting expeditions.

06:09.530 --> 06:11.500
I'd be more than
happy for the help.

06:11.530 --> 06:14.700
We could all
fight Titans together.

06:14.740 --> 06:16.240
Well, you know.

06:16.270 --> 06:18.000
There's our work
in the interior, so...

06:18.040 --> 06:20.870
[MALE SOLDIER 33E] Hey!
The advance squad is back!

06:20.910 --> 06:23.440
Go! Tell Commander Pyxis!

06:23.480 --> 06:26.280
[PHIL panting]

06:26.310 --> 06:30.920
[PYXIS] I see. No breach as far
as you could tell, correct?

06:30.950 --> 06:32.850
[PHIL]
That's correct, sir!

06:32.890 --> 06:35.690
[PYXIS]
Mmm. As I thought.

06:37.830 --> 06:41.460
But, sir! A situation
has developed!

06:41.500 --> 06:43.330
You see, we ran
into another group

06:43.360 --> 06:44.760
on the way back to Trost.

06:44.800 --> 06:47.800
It was the Scout unit led
by Section Commander Hange.

06:47.840 --> 06:49.940
There were recruits
from the 104th Cadet Corps

06:49.970 --> 06:52.370
with them, none of whom
had equipment.

06:52.410 --> 06:55.270
This may sound crazy, sir,
but three of them

06:55.310 --> 06:56.980
were Titans!

06:57.010 --> 06:59.880
--[SOLDIERS gasp]
--What the--? Hang on sec.

06:59.910 --> 07:03.880
Seriously? You mean like
there were three... more?

07:03.920 --> 07:07.450
But... who were they?
Who, damn it?

07:07.490 --> 07:09.390
Actually, I, um...

07:09.420 --> 07:11.790
Jean, calm down.

07:11.830 --> 07:14.560
What happened when their
Titan forms were revealed?

07:14.600 --> 07:16.000
The Scouts engaged
the Armored Titan

07:16.030 --> 07:19.630
and the Colossal in battle
as best they could, sir!

07:19.670 --> 07:21.770
But by the time our unit
arrived on the scene

07:21.800 --> 07:24.240
it was... too late.

07:24.270 --> 07:25.840
I'm sorry.

07:36.750 --> 07:43.260
[footsteps]

07:43.290 --> 07:45.260
[HANNES sighs]

07:45.290 --> 07:47.630
Oh, man. What a mess.

07:47.660 --> 07:51.660
Count your lucky stars
we were all the way up here.

07:51.700 --> 07:54.400
Rest of 'em got blasted
by steam and debris;

07:54.440 --> 07:56.700
nothing much they could do.

07:59.340 --> 08:01.510
How badly is Mikasa hurt?

08:01.540 --> 08:03.640
Well there aren't
any wounds to speak of.

08:03.710 --> 08:06.250
I think it's just a concussion.

08:06.280 --> 08:07.910
Could be worse.

08:09.680 --> 08:12.820
[HANNES] Armin, I've got
food if you're hungry.

08:12.850 --> 08:14.620
You eaten?

08:17.930 --> 08:19.260
[HANNES]
Be right back.

08:30.430 --> 08:33.470
[Indistinctive chatter]

08:33.500 --> 08:37.970
[ARMIN panting]

08:38.010 --> 08:40.210
[ARMIN]
Mikasa!

08:40.240 --> 08:42.580
[Panting]

08:42.610 --> 08:45.410
Come quick!
Eren's in trouble!

08:45.450 --> 08:47.680
What kind of trouble?

08:47.720 --> 08:49.680
It's those
three bullies again.

08:49.720 --> 08:52.190
They took the bread
I just bought.

08:52.220 --> 08:55.620
I--I told Eren about it and--

08:55.660 --> 08:59.030
I didn't want him to go!

08:59.060 --> 09:00.530
Wait!

09:01.330 --> 09:02.930
Give it back.

09:02.970 --> 09:04.630
You have dirt in
your ears or somethin'?

09:04.670 --> 09:07.270
Like I said, I already
ate the whole thing.

09:07.300 --> 09:08.400
Tasty.

09:08.440 --> 09:10.970
But that was three days
worth of food for them!

09:11.010 --> 09:12.070
You gotta be kiddin' me.

09:12.110 --> 09:14.440
Those table scraps?

09:14.480 --> 09:17.350
Knock it off.
You'll make me feel bad.

09:17.380 --> 09:19.650
Whatever, you want it
back so damn much--

09:19.680 --> 09:23.520
--[Imitates retching]
--[BOY 33C, 33B laugh]

09:23.550 --> 09:26.390
Pay him back
what the bread was worth!

09:27.990 --> 09:31.360
[Grunts]

09:31.390 --> 09:32.990
Whoa! What are you doing?

09:33.030 --> 09:35.300
Hey! There's a
situation over here

09:35.330 --> 09:36.500
if you hadn't noticed!

09:36.530 --> 09:38.300
Get off your drunk asses!

09:38.330 --> 09:41.640
Ugh, come on. They're just
kids bein' kids.

09:41.670 --> 09:43.100
Let 'em work it out.

09:43.140 --> 09:46.470
[MALE MERCHANT 33A]
They're demolishing my stall!

09:46.510 --> 09:47.980
[BOY 33A grunts]

09:48.010 --> 09:50.180
This, uh, ain't our thing.

09:50.210 --> 09:51.880
Best wait for someone
more qualified

09:51.910 --> 09:53.910
to come along and sort it out.

09:53.950 --> 09:55.520
Huh?

09:57.450 --> 09:59.320
Eren!

09:59.360 --> 10:00.960
Eat this, punk!

10:03.260 --> 10:04.390
[BOY 33A groans]

10:04.430 --> 10:06.890
[Yells]

10:06.930 --> 10:10.230
[ALL laugh]

10:10.270 --> 10:12.370
Mikasa--!

10:12.400 --> 10:15.270
I've got this.
What are you doing?

10:15.310 --> 10:18.240
Eren, you need to
go home and chop wood.

10:18.270 --> 10:20.340
You want your mom to get angry?

10:20.380 --> 10:23.180
You little--
Now it's a fight!

10:24.210 --> 10:26.010
[BOY 33B]
You asked for it--!

10:26.050 --> 10:28.280
No! It's okay!
She can handle it!

10:28.320 --> 10:29.980
Let go!

10:30.020 --> 10:32.850
[Yells]

10:32.890 --> 10:34.160
Oh-ho! Nice one!

10:34.190 --> 10:36.460
Don't let her
do all the work!

10:36.490 --> 10:38.390
[Groans]

10:38.460 --> 10:40.060
What was that for?

10:40.100 --> 10:41.530
Don't cheer
the little bastards on!

10:41.560 --> 10:43.160
Damn freeloaders!

10:43.200 --> 10:46.570
Freeloaders? D'you just
call us freeloaders?

10:46.600 --> 10:50.000
Hey, if the shoe fits,
shove it up your ass!

10:50.040 --> 10:51.170
You son of a--!

10:51.210 --> 10:53.910
Hey. Hey!
He's got a point, y'know.

10:53.940 --> 10:57.650
--I mean--
--[MALE MERCHANT 33A grunts]

10:57.680 --> 11:02.050
[Laughs] Heh.
That's some right arm.

11:02.090 --> 11:04.390
For a chump who runs a stall!

11:07.320 --> 11:08.990
[BOY 33A yells]

11:09.030 --> 11:11.530
[Groans]

11:14.130 --> 11:16.600
[SPECTATOR 33A]
Yeah! Get him, Hannes!

11:16.630 --> 11:17.930
[SPECTATOR 33B]
Come on, man!

11:17.970 --> 11:19.930
Don't get beat by a soldier!

11:19.970 --> 11:21.540
[MILITARY POLICEMAN 33A]
Stop it right now!

11:21.570 --> 11:23.470
What the hell
is wrong with you?

11:23.510 --> 11:24.640
Act like adults!

11:24.670 --> 11:26.570
[EREN]
Give it back!

11:26.610 --> 11:28.510
[Chuckles]

11:32.150 --> 11:34.010
Damn it!

11:35.220 --> 11:36.620
[MILITARY POLICEMAN 33A
whistles]

11:36.650 --> 11:39.190
That's enough!

11:39.220 --> 11:41.020
Uh-oh. Hey, guys?

11:41.060 --> 11:43.220
This is gettin' kinda serious.

11:44.460 --> 11:46.030
Screw this!
We're outta here!

11:46.060 --> 11:47.760
Get back here!

11:49.370 --> 11:51.030
--Where d'you think you're--
--[ARMIN] No, Eren!

11:51.070 --> 11:53.100
I don't care about
the stupid bread!

11:53.140 --> 11:54.240
Let it go!

11:54.270 --> 11:55.470
That's enough.
We're going back home

11:55.510 --> 11:57.070
right this instant.

11:57.110 --> 11:58.610
Like hell! Go without me!

11:58.640 --> 11:59.510
Eren! Wait!

11:59.540 --> 12:01.440
[MILITARY POLICEMAN 33A]
No you don't!

12:01.480 --> 12:04.210
[MIKASA]
Hold on! Eren!

12:06.420 --> 12:09.250
Eren!

12:15.120 --> 12:17.690
[Exhales]

12:21.360 --> 12:23.500
[Gasps]

12:29.940 --> 12:31.670
Mikasa.

12:31.710 --> 12:33.610
Where is Eren?
Where did he go?

12:33.640 --> 12:35.940
Whoa! Calm down!

12:35.980 --> 12:37.310
Wait! You shouldn't--!

12:37.350 --> 12:39.980
We don't know
how badly you're hurt!

12:49.730 --> 12:52.060
Where is he?

12:52.090 --> 12:54.360
Eren and Ymir were taken.

12:56.200 --> 12:59.470
They're gone. Reiner and
Bertholdt abducted them.

13:02.670 --> 13:07.410
He fought, but the
Armored Titan was just too--

13:09.110 --> 13:13.250
[ARMIN] That was
about five hours ago.

13:13.280 --> 13:15.450
Somebody's gone
after them, right?

13:15.490 --> 13:18.020
Tell me somebody
went after them.

13:22.060 --> 13:24.390
--I'm sorry.
--[MIKASA] Why not?

13:26.360 --> 13:28.200
We wanted to,
but the horses

13:28.230 --> 13:31.130
are on the
other side of the wall.

13:33.270 --> 13:35.240
Our only option is to wait.

13:35.270 --> 13:37.570
The mounts can't be hauled over
until the lifts make it here

13:37.610 --> 13:39.240
and that takes time.

13:39.280 --> 13:42.340
There's nothing else
we can do right now.

13:42.380 --> 13:44.450
Section Commander Hange
and the other officers

13:44.480 --> 13:46.450
are too injured to move.

13:46.480 --> 13:49.420
We don't have enough soldiers
to form a scouting party.

13:49.450 --> 13:52.590
Even a small one would
need more than this.

13:52.620 --> 13:55.360
We're not experienced enough.

13:55.390 --> 13:57.660
You understand?

14:03.470 --> 14:06.630
Damn it. Not this again.

14:06.670 --> 14:09.000
You feel any pain?

14:09.040 --> 14:12.540
No. I hit my head,
but I think I'm okay now.

14:12.580 --> 14:14.440
Don't worry about it.

14:14.480 --> 14:16.380
It's just...

14:16.410 --> 14:20.180
...not the first time
I've been down this road.

14:20.220 --> 14:22.520
Except when Annie took him,

14:22.550 --> 14:25.320
I didn't waste
a second. Not one.

14:27.290 --> 14:30.690
That's how Captain Levi and I
were able to get him back.

14:34.030 --> 14:38.970
But... it's already
been five hours.

14:50.110 --> 14:52.980
[MIKASA]
Hey, Armin.

14:53.020 --> 14:56.620
Why's he do it? Always leave?

14:56.650 --> 15:00.350
Always end up
someplace we're not?

15:00.390 --> 15:03.390
Yeah, it does
seem to happen a lot.

15:03.430 --> 15:07.600
Ever since we were kids Eren
liked to run off on his own.

15:07.630 --> 15:10.630
Leave us worried sick.

15:10.670 --> 15:13.230
Who knows? That's just
the sort of person

15:13.270 --> 15:16.940
he's meant to be. Maybe.

15:24.210 --> 15:26.210
[MIKASA]
I don't want much.

15:26.250 --> 15:29.620
Just to be near him.

15:34.190 --> 15:36.360
That's all.

15:47.400 --> 15:51.010
[HANNES]
Good. You're awake.

15:51.040 --> 15:54.070
Must be starving. Here.

15:55.310 --> 15:57.410
Heads up, Armin.

15:58.680 --> 16:00.310
Sorry it's only field rations,

16:00.350 --> 16:02.880
but better than nothing,
I guess.

16:08.160 --> 16:10.120
[HANNES]
Not bad. Not good either.

16:10.160 --> 16:11.990
Nothing new there.

16:15.330 --> 16:17.400
Aaah.

16:17.430 --> 16:20.270
Speaking of which,
this feels familiar, huh?

16:20.300 --> 16:22.100
You two've been
runnin' damage control

16:22.140 --> 16:24.240
for that little hothead
since the good ol' days,

16:24.270 --> 16:26.910
if I recall correctly.

16:26.940 --> 16:31.050
Doesn't seem very fair,
but what do I know?

16:31.080 --> 16:34.420
Different time, different
place, same problem.

16:34.450 --> 16:38.050
Not exactly what I'd call
a healthy relationship.

16:38.090 --> 16:39.320
Am I wrong?

16:39.360 --> 16:41.020
[Chuckles]

16:41.060 --> 16:43.460
The neighborhood bullies
weren't quite so tall,

16:43.490 --> 16:46.490
but I suppose
there are similarities.

16:46.530 --> 16:49.030
Yep. That's our Eren. Heh.

16:49.070 --> 16:51.870
Can't hold his own for shit,
but always lookin' for a fight.

16:51.900 --> 16:53.430
Five guys wanna take him on,

16:53.470 --> 16:55.270
he'd wouldn't think twice
about jumping into

16:55.300 --> 16:57.140
the fray like an idiot.

16:57.170 --> 16:58.870
By the time
Mikasa gets there

16:58.910 --> 17:03.110
or the MPs show up,
he's beaten all to hell.

17:03.150 --> 17:06.110
But you know...

17:06.150 --> 17:09.150
I may not've ever had the
privilege of seeing Eren win,

17:09.190 --> 17:12.950
but I never saw the little son
of a bitch back down either.

17:15.960 --> 17:17.260
Kid's got fire.

17:17.330 --> 17:18.960
To tell the truth,
his persistence scares

17:18.990 --> 17:21.160
the piss outta me sometimes.

17:21.200 --> 17:24.970
He gets knocked on his ass,
he gets right back up again.

17:25.000 --> 17:26.370
It's in his blood.

17:26.400 --> 17:28.270
You think he'd let himself
be snatched away

17:28.300 --> 17:30.440
without fighting
tooth and nail?

17:30.470 --> 17:32.170
Not a chance.

17:32.210 --> 17:34.980
Whatever strength
he's got left, he'll use it.

17:35.010 --> 17:37.480
What's two guys
next to a whole gang?

17:37.550 --> 17:41.080
If you can count on anything,
it's that Eren'll give 'em hell.

17:41.120 --> 17:43.920
At least till you
or me shows up to help.

17:43.950 --> 17:46.950
That's how it's
always been, right?

17:46.990 --> 17:48.690
[MIKASA gasps]

17:48.720 --> 17:50.520
[ARMIN gasps]

17:53.430 --> 17:57.430
Yes, sir. Those good ol' days
were somethin' else.

17:57.470 --> 17:59.030
'Course if you ask Eren,

17:59.070 --> 18:00.870
he'd tell ya
they were an illusion.

18:00.900 --> 18:04.100
Just us kidding ourselves.

18:04.140 --> 18:06.240
But I for one was
never happier than when

18:06.280 --> 18:11.010
folks thought of me as
a freeloading waste of space.

18:11.050 --> 18:12.910
There's not much
I wouldn't do to get us back

18:12.950 --> 18:17.850
to how things used to be.
Call me sentimental.

18:17.890 --> 18:20.050
But I'm willing
to fight for it.

18:21.690 --> 18:23.560
He needs us.

18:23.590 --> 18:25.960
Whaddya say
we stick to what we know.

18:26.000 --> 18:29.400
It ain't the good ol' days 'less
the three of you are together.

18:31.400 --> 18:32.630
[ARMIN grunts]

18:32.670 --> 18:34.940
[MIKASA grunts]

18:34.970 --> 18:36.600
[HANNES grunts]

18:58.630 --> 19:00.490
They're here.

19:00.530 --> 19:01.860
Is that?

19:01.930 --> 19:03.330
Oh, wow.

19:03.370 --> 19:05.100
[MOBLIT]
Ah!

19:05.130 --> 19:07.170
Commander Erwin!

19:07.200 --> 19:09.240
[MALE SOLDIER 33G]
With MPs!

19:11.370 --> 19:14.110
[ARMIN] Never thought they'd
ride on top of the wall.

19:14.140 --> 19:18.110
Probably the
quickest route here.

19:18.150 --> 19:21.250
For the record,
I know you won't,

19:21.280 --> 19:23.350
but I'd much prefer it
if you stayed behind.

19:23.390 --> 19:26.320
No, not happening.
Nice try, though.

19:26.360 --> 19:30.390
As long as Ymir's in danger,
nothing will keep me here.

19:30.430 --> 19:33.090
Sorry. That's just how it is.

19:33.130 --> 19:36.260
[CONNY] We're all
in this together, Armin.

19:36.300 --> 19:37.400
You're not special.

19:37.430 --> 19:40.200
Every one of us
has a reason for going.

19:40.240 --> 19:43.400
Still trying to
process mine, to be honest.

19:43.440 --> 19:45.140
I have to know why
Bertholdt and Reiner

19:45.170 --> 19:47.470
did what they did.

19:47.510 --> 19:50.410
I wanna ask while I
look them dead in the eye.

19:50.450 --> 19:52.280
[Horse neighs]

19:54.150 --> 19:55.520
Good to see you,
Commander Erwin.

19:55.550 --> 19:57.220
Glad you're here.

19:57.250 --> 19:59.050
Is the situation
still the same?

19:59.090 --> 20:00.850
--Yes, sir.
--Good.

20:00.890 --> 20:03.290
Right! Deploy the lifts!

20:03.330 --> 20:05.860
[MOBLIT shrieks]
Hange?

20:05.900 --> 20:09.430
Don't just stand there.
Gi-Give me a map.

20:13.600 --> 20:16.340
[HANGE] It's a gamble,
but the trees in this forest

20:16.370 --> 20:20.170
are massive. I say
we ride straight for it.

20:20.210 --> 20:22.410
See, even if
they had a way to cover

20:22.440 --> 20:24.140
the Armored Titan's footprints,

20:24.180 --> 20:28.420
this is almost definitely
where we would find them.

20:28.450 --> 20:30.250
Why's that?

20:30.290 --> 20:31.950
[HANGE]
They need to recoup.

20:31.990 --> 20:34.220
They have the power
to assume Titan form,

20:34.260 --> 20:38.360
but other Titans on that side of
the wall still pose a threat.

20:38.390 --> 20:40.930
Especially after
putting up such a fight.

20:40.960 --> 20:43.230
Yes, Eren was the worse for it,

20:43.270 --> 20:45.970
but they've got to be spent.

20:46.000 --> 20:48.600
Remember when Annie
went out cold?

20:48.640 --> 20:52.070
Let's suppose they're headed
somewhere beyond Wall Maria.

20:52.110 --> 20:53.940
That's not a simple hike.

20:53.980 --> 20:55.410
They'll need all
the rest they can get

20:55.440 --> 20:57.640
before covering
that kind of distance.

20:57.680 --> 21:00.910
They're in no shape
to make it in a single push.

21:00.950 --> 21:03.150
And if so, they'll want
to catch their breath

21:03.190 --> 21:06.390
somewhere other Titans
can't get to them.

21:06.420 --> 21:09.560
Odds are they'll
hold out till it gets dark.

21:34.250 --> 21:36.180
[REINER]
You're awake.

21:41.620 --> 21:43.520
[REINER]
Welcome back.

21:48.100 --> 21:50.100
[HANGE]
We have until sundown!

21:52.600 --> 21:54.570
[HANGE] If we can
reach the forest by then,

21:54.600 --> 21:58.170
we might just have
a chance to save them!

21:58.210 --> 22:00.110
[ERWIN]
Let's move!

22:13.490 --> 22:18.460
♪ Closing Song
